\caption(Both endpoints use the predictions and residuals from the same sequence of refits.)
\alttext(Two pairs of increasing curves enclose the observations. The intervals differ because the fits exclude either one row or one fold.)

> Include a test covariate's likelihood ratio

Suppose the source probability of the high-variability group is one quarter
and the target probability is three quarters. The likelihood ratios,
rescaled together, are one for the low group and nine for the high group.
The response distribution within each group stays the same between source
and target. The test-point weight contributes at positive infinity and
can make the required threshold unbounded.

```{cpp, id=weighted-intervals, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/stats/conformal_calibration.hpp>
#include <print>

int main() {
    using datamunge::stats::WeightedConformalCalibration;
    const std::vector<double> scores{.2, .3, .4, .5, .6, .7, .9, 1.1, 1.5, 2.7, 3.2, 4.0};
    const WeightedConformalCalibration ordinary(scores, std::vector<double>(scores.size(), 1));
    const WeightedConformalCalibration shifted(scores, {1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 9, 9, 9});
    constexpr double predicted = 10;
    const auto print_interval = [&](const char* mode, double radius) {
        std::println("| {} | {:.1f} | [{:.1f}, {:.1f}] |",
                     mode, radius, predicted - radius, predicted + radius);
    };
    std::println("| Calibration | Residual threshold | Prediction interval |");
    std::println("| --- | ---: | ---: |");
    print_interval("Equal weights, alpha 0.30", ordinary.threshold(1, .30));
    print_interval("Low group, alpha 0.30", shifted.threshold(1, .30));
    print_interval("High group, alpha 0.30", shifted.threshold(9, .30));
    print_interval("High group, alpha 0.10", shifted.threshold(9, .10));
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Calibration | Residual threshold | Prediction interval |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| Equal weights, alpha 0.30 | 2.7 | [7.3, 12.7] |
| Low group, alpha 0.30 | 3.2 | [6.8, 13.2] |
| High group, alpha 0.30 | 4.0 | [6.0, 14.0] |
| High group, alpha 0.10 | inf | [-inf, inf] |
